:: Church encounter - holy welcome
<h1 class="ptitle"><<cabinName>></h1>
<br /><br />
/* A kind nun meets a worker at the gate as they come back from an outside job, with water and a cool cloth. Feral nuns too. */
<<set _ce = setup.churchEncounters>>
<<set _fx = setup.nurseryEncounters>>
<<set _cast = _ce.cast()>>
<<if !_cast>>
	<<goto 'Wood cabin'>>
<<else>>
<<set _nun = _cast.nun, _worker = _cast.worker>>
<<set _feral = _ce.isFeral(_nun)>>
<<set _nunName = setup.displayName(_nun), _wName = setup.displayName(_worker)>>
<<set _nHe = setup.pronounceWhat(_nun), _nHis = setup.pronounceWhos(_nun), _nHim = setup.pronounceWho(_nun)>>
<<set _wHe = setup.pronounceWhat(_worker), _wHis = setup.pronounceWhos(_worker), _wHim = setup.pronounceWho(_worker)>>
<<set _wMc = setup.npc.mcName(_worker), _nMc = setup.npc.mcName(_nun)>>
<<set _jobs = { garden: 'the garden', forest: 'the woods', quarry: 'the quarry', scavenging: 'a long day of scavenging' }>>
<<set _labor = { garden: 'dirt under every fingernail and the sun still hot on the back of ' + _wHis + ' neck', forest: 'sawdust in ' + _wHis + ' hair and sap on ' + _wHis + ' hands', quarry: 'grey with stone dust from head to toe', scavenging: 'dusty and footsore, a heavy pack dragging at ' + _wHis + ' shoulders' }>>
<<set _likesSoda = (_worker.likes ?? []).includes('soda'), _sodaOk = !(_worker.dislikes ?? []).includes('soda') && !_worker.offeredSoda>>

<<=_wName>> trudges in through the gate from <<=_jobs[_worker.assignedTo]>>, <<=_labor[_worker.assignedTo]>>. <<=_nunName>> is waiting just inside, a bucket of water at <<=_nHis>> feet and a folded cloth over <<=_nHis>> arm.
<br /><br />
<<if _feral>>
	<<sayFeral _nun>>trots to meet <<=_wName>>, takes the pack off <<=_wHis>> shoulders before <<=_wHe>> can protest, and pushes a dipper of water into <<=_wHis>> hands, watching until <<=_wHe>> drinks<</sayFeral>>
	<br />
	<<=_nunName>> soaks the cloth, wrings it out and presses it to the back of <<=_wName>>'s neck, then sniffs critically at <<=_wHis>> hands and starts scrubbing them clean as well, with great seriousness and no regard at all for <<=_wName>>'s dignity.
	<br /><br />
	<<sayNpc _worker>>
		Alright, alright! I can wash my own hands. <<=ucfirst(_wMc)>>, is <<=_nHe>> always like this?
	<</sayNpc>>
	<br />
	<<=ucfirst(_wHe)>> is laughing, though, and <<=_wHe>> doesn't pull away.
<<else>>
	<<sayNpc _nun>>
		Welcome home. Here, drink this first, slowly. Then sit for a minute, the rest of the evening can wait for you.
	<</sayNpc>>
	<br />
	<<=_nunName>> lifts the pack from <<=_wName>>'s shoulders, puts a dipper of water in <<=_wHis>> hands and lays the cool, wet cloth across the back of <<=_wHis>> neck. <<=_wName>> closes <<=_wHis>> eyes and sighs.
	<br /><br />
	<<sayNpc _worker>>
		You have no idea how good that feels. <<=ucfirst(_wMc)>>, whoever thought of this deserves a medal.
	<</sayNpc>>
	<br />
	<<sayNpc _nun>>
		It's no more than the holy texts ask of us, <<=_nMc>>. The ones who carry the heaviest loads should be the first ones cared for.
	<</sayNpc>>
<</if>>
<br />

<div id="ce_choices">
	<<if _sodaOk>>
		<<set _sodaLabel = 'Offer ' + _wHim + ' a soda'>>
		<<if setup.cabinInventory.has('soda')>>
			<<link _sodaLabel>>
				<<replace '#ce_choices'>>
					<<run setup.cabinInventory.drop('soda')>>
					<<set _worker.offeredSoda = true>>
					<<set _sodaGain = _likesSoda ? 2 : 1>>
					<<run _ce.byNun(_nun, _worker, 'happy', 1 + _sodaGain, 2 + _sodaGain)>>
					<<run _fx.change(_worker, 'relationship', 2, 4)>>
					<<run _fx.change(_nun, 'relationship', 1, 2)>>
					<<run _ce.changeToward(_nun, _worker, 2, 2)>>
					<<run _ce.changeToward(_worker, _nun, 4, 4)>>
					<<if _likesSoda>><<run _ce.boostWork(_worker)>><</if>>
					You fish a soda out of your pack and hand it over. <<=_wName>> cracks it open and drinks half of it in one go<<if _likesSoda>>, and then grins at you like you've handed <<=_wHim>> treasure<</if>>.
					<br /><br />
					<<sayNpc _worker>>
						<<if _likesSoda>>
							Oh, that's the good stuff. Thank you, <<=_wMc>>. I feel like I could go back out there and do it all again.
						<<else>>
							Thanks, <<=_wMc>>. That hits the spot.
						<</if>>
					<</sayNpc>>
					<br />
					<<if _feral>>
						<<sayFeral _nun>>looks from the can to you, then bumps <<=_nHis>> head against your shoulder, the way <<=_nHe>> does when <<=_nHe>> approves of something<</sayFeral>>
					<<else>>
						<<sayNpc _nun>>
							Thank you, <<=_nMc>>. It means more coming from you. People learn kindness by watching it done.
						<</sayNpc>>
					<</if>>
					<br />
					[[Continue|Wood cabin]]
					<<nurseryEffects>>
					<<if _likesSoda>><<linkdesc>><<=_wName>> will bring in a little extra from <<=_jobs[_worker.assignedTo]>> tonight<</linkdesc>><</if>>
				<</replace>>
			<</link>>
		<<else>>
			<div class="link-internal" style="background: #ccc"><<=_sodaLabel>> (you have none)</div>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
	<<set _drinkLabel = 'Offer ' + _wHim + ' an energy drink'>>
	<<if setup.cabinInventory.has('energy_drink')>>
		<<link _drinkLabel>>
			<<replace '#ce_choices'>>
				<<run setup.cabinInventory.drop('energy_drink')>>
				<<run _ce.byNun(_nun, _worker, 'happy', 3, 4)>>
				<<run _fx.change(_worker, 'relationship', 2, 4)>>
				<<run _fx.change(_nun, 'relationship', 1, 2)>>
				<<run _ce.changeToward(_nun, _worker, 2, 2)>>
				<<run _ce.changeToward(_worker, _nun, 4, 4)>>
				<<run _ce.boostWork(_worker)>>
				You hand <<=_wName>> an energy drink. <<=ucfirst(_wHe)>> makes a face at the first sip, then drains the rest, and you can practically watch the life come back into <<=_wHim>>.
				<br /><br />
				<<sayNpc _worker>>
					Whoa. Okay. That's working. Thanks, <<=_wMc>>, I think I just got my second wind.
				<</sayNpc>>
				<br />
				<<if _feral>>
					<<sayFeral _nun>>looks from the empty can to you, then bumps <<=_nHis>> head against your shoulder, the way <<=_nHe>> does when <<=_nHe>> approves of something<</sayFeral>>
				<<else>>
					<<sayNpc _nun>>
						Thank you, <<=_nMc>>. It means more coming from you. People learn kindness by watching it done.
					<</sayNpc>>
				<</if>>
				<br />
				[[Continue|Wood cabin]]
				<<nurseryEffects>>
				<<linkdesc>><<=_wName>> will bring in a little extra from <<=_jobs[_worker.assignedTo]>> tonight<</linkdesc>>
			<</replace>>
		<</link>>
	<<else>>
		<div class="link-internal" style="background: #ccc"><<=_drinkLabel>> (you have none)</div>
	<</if>>
	<<link 'Leave them to it'>>
		<<replace '#ce_choices'>>
			<<run _ce.byNun(_nun, _worker, 'happy', 1, 2)>>
			<<run _ce.changeToward(_nun, _worker, 2, 2)>>
			<<run _ce.changeToward(_worker, _nun, 4, 4)>>
			<<sayNpc _worker>>
				Evening, <<=_wMc>>. Don't worry about me, I'm in good hands.
			<</sayNpc>>
			<br />
			You give them a nod and leave them to it. When you look back from the cabin door, <<=_wName>> is sitting on an upturned crate with the cloth over <<=_wHis>> face, and <<=_nunName>> is <<if _feral>>curled at <<=_wHis>> feet, keeping watch<<else>>refilling <<=_wHis>> water<</if>>.
			<br /><br />
			[[Continue|Wood cabin]]
			<<nurseryEffects>>
		<</replace>>
	<</link>>
</div>
<</if>>
